  "question": {
    "text": "Sodium oxide reacts with water to produce sodium hydroxide. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of sodium oxide is dissolved in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of water. Neglecting the change in volume, the concentration of the resulting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math> solution is _________&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;(Nearest integer)<br />[Atomic mass : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Na</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math>]"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "13",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>NaOH</mi></math><br />According to reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>62</mn></mfrac></math> mole of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>40</mn><mn>62</mn></mfrac></math> mole of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math><br />so molarity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math> solution is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi>NaOH</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mi>ml</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>40</mn><mn>62</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1000</mn><mn>500</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>80</mn><mn>62</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>29</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>"
  }
